cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying paper."
type: software
title: "ORBIT: Orthogonal Rotation for Biological Inter-species Transfer"
abstract: >
  Cross-species alignment of gene network embeddings by a closed-form orthogonal Procrustes
  rotation anchored on ortholog pairs. Each species is rotated onto a reference with one SVD;
  the rotation has no hyperparameters, needs no training and preserves within-species geometry
  exactly. On coexpression networks of 153 plant species ORBIT separates orthologs from
  non-orthologs better than an autoencoder retrained on the same embeddings (AUROC 0.67 vs 0.55)
  and aligns all species in 2.7 minutes on CPU; on the STRING protein interaction embeddings of
  1,322 eukaryotes it matches the published SPACE embeddings on their own benchmarks.
